# Magnetic Field Analysis in NGC 6946: Radio and FIR Comparison

This project utilizes data from the VLA (Very Large Array) and SOFIA (Stratospheric Observatory for Infrared Astronomy) to study and compare the magnetic fields of the galaxy NGC 6946 in the radio and FIR regimes.

## Objectives

- Investigate the properties of magnetic fields in NGC 6946 across different wavelengths.
- Analyze correlations between astrophysical parameters such as:
  - Star formation rate (SFR)
  - Column density
  - Polarization intensity
  - Polarization fraction

## Progress

- Data from both radio (VLA) and FIR (SOFIA) have been processed and compared.
- Initial correlations between SFR, column density, and polarization properties have been analyzed.

## Future Work

- Extend the analysis to explore additional parameters.
- Refine methodologies for better understanding the magnetic field's role in galaxy dynamics.
- Publish findings and share scripts for community use.

